A: In order to check your arraylist with Pex, you must have a class that has a method that calls your ArrayList function. 
For instance, if you have some class like this:
public class ClassUnderTest 
{
    ArrayList arrList;

    [PexMethod]
    public void MyMethodUnderTest([PexAssumeValid] ArrayList arrList) 
    {
        this.arrList = arrList;
        // Call ArrayList method here
    }
}

The Pex approach will try to cover as many possible cases as it can using the [PexMethod] attribute on the MyMethodUnderTest, and using the [PexAssumeValid] attribute on the arrList parameter which tells Pex that the input list is valid and will not crash your application.
Once your tests are completed, you can review them and fix any where something is not as expected.
Hope this helps,
Best Regards,
Sandip Kumar 

